# Database Object Naming

When designing or changing PDManer models, Schema/data-change SQL, DataObject/Mapper mappings, or database tests:

- Each database-owning project keeps exactly one canonical model at `docs/database/<service-short-name>.pdma.json`; use a lowercase, no-space kebab-case filename such as `finance.pdma.json`.
- The model's internal `name`/`describe` may be descriptive but never changes the canonical filename. Reconcile useful changes from PDManer Save-As files into the short-name model, then remove the duplicate; `.back_*` files remain ignored local backups.
- Every physical table name must be lowercase `snake_case` and start with `t_`, for example `t_party`.
- Every unique index name must start with `uk_`.
- Every non-unique index name must start with `idx_`.
- DataObject types use business entity names inside the `dataobject` package and never add a `DO` suffix.
- Chinese PDManer `defName` values remain business-readable and do not receive technical prefixes.
- Architecture prose and logical catalogs may omit `t_`; PDManer `defKey`, manually maintained SQL and mappings must use the physical table name.
- Reject `ix_` for new or regenerated ordinary indexes.
